{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metadata and accept ","type":"text"},{"code":"AuthnRequest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s on ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/saml\/v2\/{tenant}\/{metadata,sso,slo}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Off","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unless an organization turns it on.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A SAML IdP issues assertions that other systems","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accept as proof of identity, so a deployment that has never decided to be one issues","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none, and the three endpoints answer ","type":"text"},{"code":"404","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as if they did not exist. The switch lives on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this policy, beside the other OpenID Provider surface controls, because the SSO endpoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the same browser login hop and OP session with a different wire format.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Disable-only","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", with the shape of [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]: a tenant may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turn its organization’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" off but never its ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on, because the decision to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"issue identity assertions on behalf of the organization’s tenants is the organization’s.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A deployment built without the ","type":"text"},{"code":"saml","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" feature answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"404","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whatever this says; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"setting is a capability, not a grant (each SP must still be registered, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"allow_idp_initiated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is its own opt-in).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/samlIdpEnabled","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"samlIdpEnabled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/SE":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Encodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy":{"abstract":[{"text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is which is the whole of what [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_tenant_override"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clamp_overrides_to_org"},{"type":"text","text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"], validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the mirror image of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoi